          "text": "In AP English Language, a paragraph is not merely a visual indent; it is a rhetorical container intended to develop a single logical idea. Before analyzing arrangement, students must recognize that transitions signal the relationship between ideas (contrast, addition, causation). A coherent paragraph requires a clear topic sentence that governs the evidence and a closing or transitional statement that bridges to the next unit of thought. Without understanding the intended function of each component, analyzing its arrangement is impossible, as form is always in service of logical progression. The reader's path depends on how well these micro-units are connected, creating a chain of reasoning that feels inevitable rather than disjointed."
