          "text": "To revise for precise style, begin by isolating sentences where the argument feels diffuse or abstract. Identify weak verbs, passive constructions, and nominalizations that drain the prose of energy. Next, examine how syntactic choices—such as periodic versus cumulative sentences—dictate pacing and focal points. Ask what specific emotion or logical conclusion the author intends to provoke at that exact moment. Replace ambiguous phrasing with concrete, sensory-laden diction that aligns with the overarching persona. Finally, verify that transitions between clauses reflect genuine logical relationships rather than mechanical sequencing."
